    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a high-ceiling slate today, anchored by the elite 83.29 rating of **Gunnar Henderson**. Facing the vulnerable arm of Randy V\u00e1squez (4.89 xERA), **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from both a favorable park shift and a significant skill advantage, making him our highest-scoring play. Following closely, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) is a prime target against Trey Gibson. The combination of Gibson\u2019s 5.87 xERA and the plus-hitting environment suggests a massive afternoon for the Waves\u2019 core, supported further by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who earns a 72.20 rating by leveraging a dynamic platoon advantage against Luis Castillo.\n\nWhile the lineup is optimized for scoring, we must navigate several high-risk matchups. **Sam Antonacci** (45.30) draws the toughest assignment of the day against Yoshinobu Yamamoto; he remains active primarily due to his critical stolen base profile, though he remains a candidate to be pulled if the game gets out of hand. On the bench, **Nasim Nunez** (53.59) was the final cut for the starting nine. While **Nasim Nunez** offers premium speed, he was ultimately pushed out by the higher base-power projections of our corner infielders, though his elite stolen base potential keeps him as a high-priority sub if we need to manufacture runs late. \n\nOwners should monitor the final lineups closely, as many of these scores are built on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. **Kyle Tucker** (67.23) and **Andy Pages** (62.03) provide solid secondary support against Sean Burke, maintaining high floors in the middle of our order. We are essentially betting on the volatility of V\u00e1squez and Gibson to carry the day, but with **Josh Jung** (55.26) facing the sturdy Ranger Suarez, we have enough depth to bridge the gap if our primary targets encounter early resistance.",
